<td id="S3.T2.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:-0.1pt 4.0pt;"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Answer</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding:-0.1pt 4.0pt;"><math id="S3.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if the final answer
the predicted coordination <math id="S3.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{x},\hat{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{x},\hat{y})</annotation></semantics></math> lies inside the <math id="S3.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S3.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},y_{1},x_{2},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},y_{1},x_{2},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S3.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</td>
